IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P7-gates`

-- P7-testing: Articles 60, 60a and 61 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744):
-- testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes, the same under Section B of Annex I (inserted by the Omnibus),
-- and the informed consent of the subjects. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Group `General`: Chapter VI applies from 2 August 2026.
-- Seams: S1 (the route by which the AI system is high-risk), S6 (Articles 43, 47, 48, 49 are not needed here), S7 (this module answers
-- "all the conditions laid down in Article 57 or 60 are fulfilled" for the keel's Art 3(57): `Art 60(4) the testing in real world conditions may be conducted`),
-- S14 (Art 2(2)). Names that come from other parts' provisions (Articles 49, 71, 73, 13, 75) are plain facts asked as BOOLEAN or NUMBER inputs.
-- The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 60 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 60 provider or prospective provider`
    `Art 60 Member State`

DECLARE `Art 60 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 60a(3) notify the Commission of the real-world testing framework`
    `Art 61(1) obtain the informed consent of the subject`

§ `Article 60(1) and (2): who may test in real world conditions outside the sandboxes (as enacted and as amended)`

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1498 | 1. Testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes may be conducted by providers or prospective providers of high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III, in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan referred to in this Article, without prejudice to the prohibitions under Article 5.
@ref Art 60(1) first subparagraph as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1498)
GIVEN `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(1) as enacted the provider may conduct testing in real world conditions outside the sandboxes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
    WHEN `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` THEN IF `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- the grant: "may be conducted by providers or prospective providers of high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III, in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan". NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant names high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III only as enacted; a system under Article 6(1) with Annex I is outside it

-- src:931 | 1. Testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes may be conducted by providers or prospective providers of high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III or covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan referred to in this Article, without prejudice to the prohibitions under Article 5.
@ref Art 60(1) first subparagraph as amended (src:931)
GIVEN `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(1) as amended the provider may conduct testing in real world conditions outside the sandboxes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
    WHEN `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` THEN IF `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- the grant: "high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III or covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan". NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan"
    WHEN `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` THEN IF `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` AND `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- the grant for a system covered by Section A of Annex I. NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I" (a Section B product is for Article 60a)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant names high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III or covered by Section A of Annex I

@ref Art 60(1) first subparagraph (gate, then the version in force; src:931)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(1) the provider may conduct testing in real world conditions outside the sandboxes` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 57 Article 2(2) leaves the provision to apply` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 60 "" 1) THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (S14: Article 60 is not on that list; the keel answered JUST FALSE)
         ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
              WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 60(1) as enacted the provider may conduct testing in real world conditions outside the sandboxes` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan`  -- VERSION as enacted
              WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 60(1) as amended the provider may conduct testing in real world conditions outside the sandboxes` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan`  -- VERSION as amended

-- src:931 | 1. Testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes may be conducted by providers or prospective providers of high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III or covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan referred to in this Article, without prejudice to the prohibitions under Article 5.
@ref Art 60(1) first subparagraph (without prejudice to Article 5) (src:931)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the prohibition is one under Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(1) the testing prejudices the prohibitions under Article 5` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the prohibition is one under Article 5` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without prejudice to the prohibitions under Article 5"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision speaks only of the case it names

-- src:933 | The Commission shall, by means of implementing acts, specify the detailed elements of the real-world testing plan. Those implementing acts shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2).
@ref Art 60(1) second subparagraph (src:933)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission specifies the detailed elements of the real-world testing plan by means of implementing acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those implementing acts are adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(1) the Commission has specified the detailed elements of the real-world testing plan by implementing acts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Commission specifies the detailed elements of the real-world testing plan by means of implementing acts` AND `those implementing acts are adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission shall, by means of implementing acts, specify the detailed elements of the real-world testing plan. Those implementing acts shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)"

-- src:934 | This paragraph shall be without prejudice to Union or national law on the testing in real world conditions of high-risk AI systems related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I.
@ref Art 60(1) third subparagraph (src:934)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the law is Union or national law on the testing in real world conditions of high-risk AI systems related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(1) this paragraph prejudices Union or national law on the testing of high-risk AI systems related to products covered by Annex I` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the law is Union or national law on the testing in real world conditions of high-risk AI systems related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph shall be without prejudice to Union or national law on the testing in real world conditions of high-risk AI systems related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision speaks only of the case it names

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1501 | 2. Providers or prospective providers may conduct testing of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III in real world conditions at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system on their own or in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers.
@ref Art 60(2) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1501)
GIVEN `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the testing is at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is on the provider's own account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(2) as enacted the provider may conduct testing at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
    WHEN `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` THEN IF `the testing is at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system` AND (`the testing is on the provider's own account` OR `the testing is in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- the grant: "at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system on their own or in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers". NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at any time before the placing on the market"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant names high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III only as enacted

-- src:936 | 2. Providers or prospective providers may conduct testing of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III or covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I in real world conditions at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the high-risk AI system on their own or in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers.
@ref Art 60(2) as amended (src:936)
GIVEN `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is on the provider's own account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(2) as amended the provider may conduct testing at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
    WHEN `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` THEN IF `the testing is at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system` AND (`the testing is on the provider's own account` OR `the testing is in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- the grant: "at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the high-risk AI system on their own or in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers". NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at any time before the placing on the market"
    WHEN `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` THEN IF `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` AND `the testing is at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system` AND (`the testing is on the provider's own account` OR `the testing is in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- the grant for a system covered by Section A of Annex I. NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant names high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III or covered by Section A of Annex I

@ref Art 60(2) (gate, then the version in force; src:936)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is on the provider's own account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(2) the provider may conduct testing at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 57 Article 2(2) leaves the provision to apply` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 60 "" 2) THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (S14: Article 60 is not on that list; the keel answered JUST FALSE)
         ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
              WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 60(2) as enacted the provider may conduct testing at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the testing is at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system` `the testing is on the provider's own account` `the testing is in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers`  -- VERSION as enacted
              WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 60(2) as amended the provider may conduct testing at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` `the testing is at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system` `the testing is on the provider's own account` `the testing is in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers`  -- VERSION as amended

-- src:938 | 3. The testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions under this Article shall be without prejudice to any ethical review that is required by Union or national law.
@ref Art 60(3) (src:938)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `an ethical review is required by Union or national law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60(3) the testing prejudices an ethical review required by Union or national law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `an ethical review is required by Union or national law` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions under this Article shall be without prejudice to any ethical review that is required by Union or national law"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision speaks only of the case it names

§ `Article 60(4): the conditions (a) to (k), each a function, and the whole`

-- src:940 | (a) the provider or prospective provider has drawn up a real-world testing plan and submitted it to the market surveillance authority in the Member State where the testing in real world conditions is to be conducted;
@ref Art 60(4)(a) (src:940)
GIVEN `the provider or prospective provider has drawn up a real-world testing plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan has been submitted to the market surveillance authority in the Member State where the testing in real world conditions is to be conducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 60(4)(a) the real-world testing plan has been drawn up and submitted` MEANS
    `the provider or prospective provider has drawn up a real-world testing plan`
    AND `the plan has been submitted to the market surveillance authority in the Member State where the testing in real world conditions is to be conducted`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only where all of the following conditions are met"

-- src:941 | (b) the market surveillance authority in the Member State where the testing in real world conditions is to be conducted has approved the testing in real world conditions and the real-world testing plan; where the market surveillance authority has not provided an answer within 30 days, the testing in real world conditions and the real-world testing plan shall be understood to have been approved; where national law does not provide for a tacit approval, the testing in real world conditions shall remain subject to an authorisation;
@ref Art 60(4)(b) (src:941)
GIVEN `the market surveillance authority has approved the testing in real world conditions and the real-world testing plan, expressly or by an authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has provided an answer within 30 days of the submission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `national law provides for a tacit approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the plan was submitted` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 60(4)(b) the market surveillance authority has approved the testing and the plan` MEANS
        `the market surveillance authority has approved the testing in real world conditions and the real-world testing plan, expressly or by an authorisation`
    OR (    `national law provides for a tacit approval`
        AND NOT `the market surveillance authority has provided an answer within 30 days of the submission`
        AND ((Day `the date asked`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the plan was submitted`)) GREATER THAN 30)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the market surveillance authority has not provided an answer within 30 days, the testing ... shall be understood to have been approved; where national law does not provide for a tacit approval, the testing in real world conditions shall remain subject to an authorisation"

-- src:942 | (c) the provider or prospective provider, with the exception of providers or prospective providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in points 1, 6 and 7 of Annex III in the areas of law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control management, and high-risk AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III has registered the testing in real world conditions in accordance with Article 71(4) with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified in Annex IX; the provider or prospective provider of high-risk AI systems referred to in points 1, 6 and 7 of Annex III in the areas of law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control management, has registered the testing in real-world conditions in the secure non-public section of the EU database according to Article 49(4), point (d), with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified therein; the provider or prospective provider of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III has registered the testing in real-world conditions in accordance with Article 49(5);
@ref Art 60(4)(c) (src:942)
GIVEN `the AI system is referred to in points 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III in the areas of law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control management` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is referred to in point 2 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 71(4) with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified in Annex IX` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing has been registered in the secure non-public section of the EU database according to Article 49(4), point (d), with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified therein` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 49(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 60(4)(c) the testing in real world conditions has been registered as the text requires` MEANS
    IF `the AI system is referred to in points 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III in the areas of law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control management`
    THEN `the testing has been registered in the secure non-public section of the EU database according to Article 49(4), point (d), with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified therein`
    ELSE IF `the AI system is referred to in point 2 of Annex III`
         THEN `the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 49(5)`
         ELSE `the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 71(4) with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified in Annex IX`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only where all of the following conditions are met"

-- src:943 | (d) the provider or prospective provider conducting the testing in real world conditions is established in the Union or has appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union;
@ref Art 60(4)(d) (src:943)
GIVEN `the provider or prospective provider conducting the testing is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider or prospective provider has appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 60(4)(d) the provider is established in the Union or has appointed a legal representative established in the Union` MEANS
    `the provider or prospective provider conducting the testing is established in the Union`
    OR `the provider or prospective provider has appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only where all of the following conditions are met"

-- src:944 | (e) data collected and processed for the purpose of the testing in real world conditions shall be transferred to third countries only provided that appropriate and applicable safeguards under Union law are implemented;
@ref Art 60(4)(e) (src:944)
GIVEN `data collected and processed for the purpose of the testing are transferred to third countries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appropriate and applicable safeguards under Union law are implemented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 60(4)(e) data are transferred to third countries only with appropriate safeguards` MEANS
    NOT `data collected and processed for the purpose of the testing are transferred to third countries`
    OR `appropriate and applicable safeguards under Union law are implemented`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be transferred to third countries only provided that appropriate and applicable safeguards under Union law are implemented"

-- src:945 | (f) the testing in real world conditions does not last longer than necessary to achieve its objectives and in any case not longer than six months, which may be extended for an additional period of six months, subject to prior notification by the provider or prospective provider to the market surveillance authority, accompanied by an explanation of the need for such an extension;
@ref Art 60(4)(f) (src:945)
GIVEN `the testing does not last longer than necessary to achieve its objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the testing began` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the testing ended or is asked about` IS A DATE
      `the testing has been extended for an additional period of six months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider or prospective provider notified the market surveillance authority beforehand, with an explanation of the need for the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 60(4)(f) the testing does not last longer than the text allows` MEANS
        `the testing does not last longer than necessary to achieve its objectives`
    AND (   `the date on which the testing ended or is asked about` AT MOST (`add months` `the date on which the testing began` 6)
         OR (    `the testing has been extended for an additional period of six months`
             AND `the provider or prospective provider notified the market surveillance authority beforehand, with an explanation of the need for the extension`
             AND `the date on which the testing ended or is asked about` AT MOST (`add months` `the date on which the testing began` 12)))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not longer than necessary ... and in any case not longer than six months, which may be extended for an additional period of six months, subject to prior notification"

-- src:946 | (g) the subjects of the testing in real world conditions who are persons belonging to vulnerable groups due to their age or disability, are appropriately protected;
@ref Art 60(4)(g) (src:946)
GIVEN `some of the subjects of the testing belong to vulnerable groups due to their age or disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those subjects are appropriately protected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 60(4)(g) the subjects who belong to vulnerable groups are appropriately protected` MEANS
    NOT `some of the subjects of the testing belong to vulnerable groups due to their age or disability`
    OR `those subjects are appropriately protected`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the subjects ... who are persons belonging to vulnerable groups due to their age or disability, are appropriately protected"

-- src:947 | (h) where a provider or prospective provider organises the testing in real world conditions in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers, the latter have been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to their decision to participate, and given the relevant instructions for use of the AI system referred to in Article 13; the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer shall conclude an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities with a view to ensuring compliance with the provisions for testing in real world conditions under this Regulation and under other applicable Union and national law;
@ref Art 60(4)(h) (src:947)
GIVEN `the provider or prospective provider organises the testing in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployers or prospective deployers have been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to their decision to participate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployers or prospective deployers have been given the relevant instructions for use of the AI system referred to in Article 13` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer have concluded an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 60(4)(h) the deployers taking part have been informed and an agreement concluded` MEANS
    NOT `the provider or prospective provider organises the testing in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers`
    OR (    `the deployers or prospective deployers have been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to their decision to participate`
        AND `the deployers or prospective deployers have been given the relevant instructions for use of the AI system referred to in Article 13`
        AND `the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer have concluded an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a provider or prospective provider organises the testing ... in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers, the latter have been informed ... and the provider ... and the deployer ... shall conclude an agreement"

-- src:948 | (i) the subjects of the testing in real world conditions have given informed consent in accordance with Article 61, or in the case of law enforcement, where the seeking of informed consent would prevent the AI system from being tested, the testing itself and the outcome of the testing in the real world conditions shall not have any negative effect on the subjects, and their personal data shall be deleted after the test is performed;
@ref Art 60(4)(i) (src:948)
GIVEN `the subjects of the testing have given informed consent in accordance with Article 61` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is in the case of law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seeking of informed consent would prevent the AI system from being tested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing itself and the outcome of the testing have no negative effect on the subjects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data of the subjects are deleted after the test is performed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 60(4)(i) the subjects have given informed consent, or the law enforcement exception applies` MEANS
        `the subjects of the testing have given informed consent in accordance with Article 61`
    OR (    `the testing is in the case of law enforcement`
        AND `the seeking of informed consent would prevent the AI system from being tested`
        AND `the testing itself and the outcome of the testing have no negative effect on the subjects`
        AND `the personal data of the subjects are deleted after the test is performed`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the subjects ... have given informed consent in accordance with Article 61, or in the case of law enforcement, where the seeking of informed consent would prevent the AI system from being tested, the testing itself and the outcome ... shall not have any negative effect on the subjects, and their personal data shall be deleted after the test is performed"

-- src:949 | (j) the testing in real world conditions is effectively overseen by the provider or prospective provider, as well as by deployers or prospective deployers through persons who are suitably qualified in the relevant field and have the necessary capacity, training and authority to perform their tasks;
