§ `Article 60a: testing under Section B of Annex I (inserted by the Omnibus)`

-- src:959 | 1. Member States may allow, in accordance with this Article, the testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes by providers or prospective providers of AI enabled products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, with a view to assessing and verifying the conformity of those systems with the requirements laid down in Articles 8 to 15.
@ref Art 60a(1) (src:959)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is by providers or prospective providers of AI enabled products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testing is with a view to assessing and verifying the conformity of those systems with the requirements laid down in Articles 8 to 15` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60a(1) the Member State may allow the testing outside the sandboxes of AI-enabled products covered by Section B of Annex I` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`Art 57 Article 2(2) leaves the provision to apply` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 60 "a" 1) THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (S14: the keel's `Art 2(2)` answered JUST FALSE)
        IF `the testing is of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes` AND `the testing is by providers or prospective providers of AI enabled products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` AND `the testing is with a view to assessing and verifying the conformity of those systems with the requirements laid down in Articles 8 to 15` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the grant: "Member States may allow, in accordance with this Article, the testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes by providers or prospective providers of AI enabled products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, with a view to assessing and verifying the conformity of those systems with the requirements laid down in Articles 8 to 15"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the case falls outside what the grant names

-- src:960 | 2. Member States that choose to allow testing as referred to in paragraph 1 shall, individually or jointly, adopt frameworks for real-world testing.
