      `the Member State chooses to allow testing as referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Member State adopts frameworks for real-world testing, individually or jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60a(2) the Member State has adopted frameworks for real-world testing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the Member State chooses to allow testing as referred to in paragraph 1`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Member States that choose to allow testing as referred to in paragraph 1"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Member State adopts frameworks for real-world testing, individually or jointly`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Member States that choose to allow testing as referred to in paragraph 1 shall, individually or jointly, adopt frameworks for real-world testing"

-- src:961 | 3. Each Member State shall notify the Commission of any real-world testing framework it adopts before implementing it. This shall not affect the competences of the Commission under the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I.
@ref Art 60a(3) first sentence (the duty to notify the Commission before implementing) (src:961)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the Member State adopts the real-world testing framework` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the Member State implements the real-world testing framework` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 60 party` `Art 60 act`
`Art 60a(3) the Member State's duty to notify the Commission of a real-world testing framework before implementing it` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Chapter VI does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Art 60 Member State`
        MUST `Art 60a(3) notify the Commission of the real-world testing framework`
        WITHIN (((Day `the date on which the Member State implements the real-world testing framework`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the Member State adopts the real-world testing framework`)) MINUS 1)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Art 60 Member State` BECAUSE "the Commission was not notified of the real-world testing framework before it was implemented"

