        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision speaks only of the case it names

-- src:962 | 4. Member States that have adopted real-world testing frameworks shall ensure that the relevant national competent authorities, relevant authorities and public authorities responsible for the management and operation of infrastructure and products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I cooperate closely with each other in good faith and remove any practical obstacles, including on procedural rules providing access to physical public infrastructure, where this is necessary, to successfully implement those real-world testing frameworks and test AI-enabled products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I.
@ref Art 60a(4) cooperation (src:962)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Member State has adopted a real-world testing framework` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Member State ensures that the relevant national competent authorities, relevant authorities and public authorities responsible for the management and operation of infrastructure and products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I cooperate closely with each other in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 60a(4) the Member State has ensured that the authorities cooperate closely and in good faith` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the Member State has adopted a real-world testing framework`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Member States that have adopted real-world testing frameworks"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Member State ensures that the relevant national competent authorities, relevant authorities and public authorities responsible for the management and operation of infrastructure and products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I cooperate closely with each other in good faith`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Member States that have adopted real-world testing frameworks shall ensure that the relevant national competent authorities, relevant authorities and public authorities ... cooperate closely with each other in good faith"

