    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the Member State has adopted a real-world testing framework` AND `removing the obstacle is necessary to successfully implement the frameworks and test AI-enabled products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where this is necessary, to successfully implement those real-world testing frameworks and test AI-enabled products"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Member State ensures that those authorities remove any practical obstacles, including on procedural rules providing access to physical public infrastructure`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Member States that have adopted real-world testing frameworks shall ensure that [those authorities] ... remove any practical obstacles, including on procedural rules providing access to physical public infrastructure, where this is necessary, to successfully implement those real-world testing frameworks and test AI-enabled products"

