§ `Article 61: informed consent to participate in testing in real world conditions outside the sandboxes`

-- src:973 | (a) the nature and objectives of the testing in real world conditions and the possible inconvenience that may be linked to their participation;
-- src:974 | (b) the conditions under which the testing in real world conditions is to be conducted, including the expected duration of the subject or subjects’ participation;
-- src:975 | (c) their rights, and the guarantees regarding their participation, in particular their right to refuse to participate in, and the right to withdraw from, testing in real world conditions at any time without any resulting detriment and without having to provide any justification;
-- src:976 | (d) the arrangements for requesting the reversal or the disregarding of the predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system;
-- src:977 | (e) the Union-wide unique single identification number of the testing in real world conditions in accordance with Article 60(4) point (c), and the contact details of the provider or its legal representative from whom further information can be obtained.
@ref Art 61(1)(a) to (e) (src:973-977)
GIVEN `the subject has been informed of the nature and objectives of the testing in real world conditions and the possible inconvenience that may be linked to their participation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subject has been informed of the conditions under which the testing is to be conducted, including the expected duration of the subject or subjects’ participation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subject has been informed of their rights, and the guarantees regarding their participation, in particular their right to refuse to participate in, and the right to withdraw from, testing at any time without any resulting detriment and without having to provide any justification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subject has been informed of the arrangements for requesting the reversal or the disregarding of the predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subject has been informed of the Union-wide unique single identification number of the testing in accordance with Article 60(4) point (c), and the contact details of the provider or its legal representative from whom further information can be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 61(1) the subject has been informed of all the matters listed` MEANS
    `the subject has been informed of the nature and objectives of the testing in real world conditions and the possible inconvenience that may be linked to their participation` AND `the subject has been informed of the conditions under which the testing is to be conducted, including the expected duration of the subject or subjects’ participation` AND `the subject has been informed of their rights, and the guarantees regarding their participation, in particular their right to refuse to participate in, and the right to withdraw from, testing at any time without any resulting detriment and without having to provide any justification` AND `the subject has been informed of the arrangements for requesting the reversal or the disregarding of the predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system` AND `the subject has been informed of the Union-wide unique single identification number of the testing in accordance with Article 60(4) point (c), and the contact details of the provider or its legal representative from whom further information can be obtained`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "freely-given informed consent shall be obtained from the subjects of testing prior to their participation in such testing and after their having been duly informed with concise, clear, relevant, and understandable information regarding: (a) ... (e)"

-- src:972 | 1. For the purpose of testing in real world conditions under Article 60, freely-given informed consent shall be obtained from the subjects of testing prior to their participation in such testing and after their having been duly informed with concise, clear, relevant, and understandable information regarding:
@ref Art 61(1) lead (src:972)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the testing is testing in real world conditions under Article 60` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent is freely given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subject was duly informed with concise, clear, relevant, and understandable information regarding the matters listed in points (a) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent was obtained prior to the subject's participation in the testing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 61(1) freely-given informed consent has been obtained from the subject prior to their participation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the testing is testing in real world conditions under Article 60`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of testing in real world conditions under Article 60"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the consent is freely given` AND `the subject was duly informed with concise, clear, relevant, and understandable information regarding the matters listed in points (a) to (e)` AND `the consent was obtained prior to the subject's participation in the testing`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purpose of testing in real world conditions under Article 60, freely-given informed consent shall be obtained from the subjects of testing prior to their participation in such testing and after their having been duly informed with concise, clear, relevant, and understandable information regarding"

-- src:972 | 1. For the purpose of testing in real world conditions under Article 60, freely-given informed consent shall be obtained from the subjects of testing prior to their participation in such testing and after their having been duly informed with concise, clear, relevant, and understandable information regarding:
@ref Art 61(1) lead (the duty to obtain the consent before the participation begins) (src:972)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the provider or prospective provider first approaches the subject to take part` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the subject's participation in the testing begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 60 party` `Art 60 act`
`Art 61(1) the provider's duty to obtain the subject's informed consent before the participation begins` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Chapter VI does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Art 60 provider or prospective provider`
        MUST `Art 61(1) obtain the informed consent of the subject`
        WITHIN (((Day `the date on which the subject's participation in the testing begins`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the provider or prospective provider first approaches the subject to take part`)) MINUS 1)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Art 60 provider or prospective provider` BECAUSE "the informed consent of the subject was not obtained before the subject began to participate in the testing"

